Z||000000||sqoach||09-11-2001||04:55 PM||||Our little town of Alva had its streets full of cars waiting in line for gas. I was lucky to get in there soon enough and fill up before the prices started to rise fast. Filled up mine, brother's car, and sister's car for $43.00. We were lucky, because as I was pumping, the trucks were there already putting up new prices. I've heard prices in OKC at $5 per gallon, and I'm sure it's much more in other areas. Two of our gas stations have ran out of unleaded that I heard of. When it's gone, it will be gone for a while. What else is going to happen? I don't know. My parents went to the store to stock up on food just in case.<BR>What is happening everywhere else??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">        <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC (FOR SALE)</FONT>||||reg||11
