Z||000010||HummelHund||09-11-2001||06:36 PM||||Just filled up my mom's Volvo just in case, gas prices haven't changed much, still about $1.30 for regular unleaded. No lines here, but I'm guessing most of the people are at the gas station on Eglin AFB, which is about 2 miles from my house, I can't go, I'm just a civilian...<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE, The "Buzz Bomb". (restoration project/daily driver)<BR>'84 SE (Dad's Project)||||reg||1
Z||000011||Pilrulz||09-11-2001||07:32 PM||||Right now on the news, many gas stations are above $5.00 in Kansas city, but one chain (QT) has sworn to stay at between $1.55 and $1.59, or where they have been all day.  Conoco has promised to revoke licenses of those conoco stations who raise prices, but they're going up anyway.  Not a problem b/c my 85 sc is filled with $1.15 reg. unl, cause i have, among other things, engine problems, and i haven't driven the car in weeks.<P>                                pil||||reg||12
Z||000012||LarryB||09-11-2001||09:02 PM||||I filled up the '86 at my favorite station near my office on the way to work this morning and just now went out and filled up my truck near home. I didn't notice any difference in prices between this morning and tonight at any of the stations (about a dozen of them) I passed; I paid $1.359 a gallon at both places, which is pretty good for metro Boston.<BR>||||reg||1
